# The patch inventory: every file outside the fork's own directories that
# differs from the postgres/postgres commit the fork last merged.
#
# Merging a new upstream release means re-examining each of these files, so
# each one is listed here with the reason the fork changes it.  The check
# in check_patch_inventory.sh fails when a changed file is missing from this
# list, when a listed file no longer differs from upstream, or when a line
# is malformed.
#
# Two kinds of line:
#
#   own   PATH
#       PATH belongs to the fork alone; nothing under it (if it ends in /)
#       or nothing at it (if it doesn't) is a core change.
#
#   patch PATH LAYER REASON...
#       PATH is a core file the fork changes.  LAYER is the roadmap layer
#       that needs the change; REASON is a one-line explanation.
#
# Blank lines and lines starting with # are ignored.  Keep each section
# sorted by path.

# The fork's own files.
own   .github/README.md
own   .github/workflows/prolly-upstream-sync.yml
own   .github/workflows/prolly.yml
own   CONTRIBUTING-prolly.md
own   contrib/prolly/
own   src/backend/prolly/
own   src/include/prolly/
own   src/test/modules/test_prolly/
own   src/test/prolly/
own   src/tools/prolly/
own   src/tools/prolly_bench/

# Core files the fork changes.
patch contrib/Makefile         0  builds the fork's extensions under contrib/prolly
patch contrib/meson.build      0  builds the fork's extensions under contrib/prolly
patch src/backend/Makefile     0  links the engine's code in src/backend/prolly into the server
patch src/backend/access/hash/hashpage.c  1a  tells the storage manager of blocks logged before they are written (smgrpreextend)
patch src/backend/access/transam/xact.c  1a  lets storage managers prepare drops before the commit record (smgrPreCommitPendingDeletes)
patch src/backend/access/transam/xlogrecovery.c  1a  skips the consistency check of a block whose storage was replaced after the record
patch src/backend/access/transam/xlogutils.c  1a  redo skips blocks whose storage was replaced after the record, and tells the storage manager before a full-page image is restored
patch src/backend/catalog/storage.c  1a  creates storage in a chosen storage manager or as a share of another relation's; truncation, drop and commit hooks for storage managers
patch src/backend/meson.build  0  links the engine's code in src/backend/prolly into the server
patch src/backend/storage/buffer/buf_init.c  1a  allocates the generations of sharing that say when cached pages must be checked again
patch src/backend/storage/buffer/bufmgr.c  1a  pages of storage that shares them are prepared (copied if shared) before they change; storage manager hooks before an asynchronous read and before extension; single-block lookups, flushes and drops
patch src/backend/storage/smgr/bulk_write.c  1a  tells the storage manager of blocks logged before they are written (smgrpreextend)
patch src/backend/storage/smgr/smgr.c  1a  storage manager interface for storage that shares pages copy-on-write; per-relation choice of implementation
patch src/include/Makefile     0  installs the engine's headers in src/include/prolly
patch src/include/access/xlogutils.h  1a  declares the redo helpers for blocks given other storage
patch src/include/catalog/storage.h  1a  declares storage creation in a chosen storage manager and as a share
patch src/include/meson.build  0  installs the engine's headers in src/include/prolly
patch src/include/storage/buf_internals.h  1a  buffer flags and generation for pages prepared before they change
patch src/include/storage/bufmgr.h  1a  declares the buffer calls for storage that shares pages
patch src/include/storage/smgr.h  1a  storage manager interface for storage that shares pages copy-on-write
patch src/test/Makefile        0  runs the requirements suite in src/test/prolly from check-world
patch src/test/meson.build     0  runs the requirements suite in src/test/prolly
patch src/test/modules/Makefile     0  builds and runs the engine's unit and conformance tests in test_prolly
patch src/test/modules/meson.build  0  builds and runs the engine's unit and conformance tests in test_prolly
